\section{What the table shows}{

\strong{Coefficient rows.} One row per coefficient, with the standard errors
the fit carries (\code{estimatr}, \code{fixest}) or those of the \code{vcov} requested
(\code{rq}). The note names the estimator.

\strong{Fixed effects.} \code{fixest} fits, and \code{estimatr} fits built with
\verb{fixed_effects =}, disclose their absorbed fixed effects as a \verb{Fixed effects:} block at the top of the fit statistics: one Yes / No row per
factor, blank for the models without the concept in a mixed table.
Varying-slope-only factors (\code{Origin[[x]]}) absorb no intercept: they read
No when another model absorbs that factor, and add no row otherwise. The
block is on by default (\code{"fixed_effects"} in \code{show_fit_stats}).

\strong{Fit statistics.} See \emph{Fit statistics} below.
}

